        "density": 0.10696,
        "chars": 60,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 6.15
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        304,
        1293,
        1830,
        1745
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "The motion picture and television industries\ncan make a substantial contribution to the economic well-\nbeing of New York City. Yet many policies and practices\nof the city government affecting these industries have\nbeen unnecessarily complicated, vexatious and time consum-\ning. The city government has thereby tended to discourage\nactivity by the motion picture and television industries\nwith the consequent injury to our economy and direct loss\nof revenue to the City of New York.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.214,
          "min": -1.3497
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 92,
          "mean": -0.0062,
          "min": -0.3874
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 91631,
        "area_px": 691278,
        "density": 0.13255,
        "chars": 481,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 5.25
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        304,
        1794,
        1880,
        2049
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Henceforth, the government of New York City\nwill make every effort to stimulate activity by the motion\npicture and television industries. All city officials are\nencouraged to examine general policies as well as individual\ndecisions in light of this goal.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2193,
          "min": -1.338
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 53,
          "mean": -0.0003,
          "min": -0.0078
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 50377,
        "area_px": 403456,
        "density": 0.12486,
        "chars": 254,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 5.04
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        295,
        2096,
        1911,
        2720
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Motion picture and television production companies\nhave been required to deal with numerous city departments\nand agencies. Although permits were issued by the Department\nof Commerce and Industrial Development, they were required\nto bear the endorsement of the Police Department, Highways\nDepartment and the Traffic Department. If wires and cables\nwere used, permission also had to be received from the\nDepartment of Water Supply, Gas and Electricity. Whenever\nParks Department property was used, a special permit was\nrequired from that Department. All of this was complicated\nmany times over by the unreasonable requirement that one\npermit be obtained for each day at each location.",
      "logprob_stats": {
